  "liner": {
   "body_md": "Mountain Goats performed at the McDonald Theatre in Eugene, Oregon, on Saturday, September 7, 2019 [1]. This concert is the 289th in the archive’s collection for the band, following a show in Seattle two days earlier [2]. The recording, taped and transferred by Liz Hamilton, captures a 96-minute set comprising 22 songs [1]. The setlist includes tracks from albums such as *In League with Dragons*, *The Sunset Tree*, and *Heretic Pride* [1]. Notable moments include the performance of “Baboon,” which was a bustout appearing for the first time in 62 archived shows, and “The Only Thing I Know,” a rare track with only four archived performances [2]. The set concludes with an encore featuring “Cotton,” “Palmcorder Yajna,” “The Diaz Brothers,” “Possum By Night,” and “This Year” [1]. A poster for the event is credited to Oregon Music News [3]. This recording is the only one available for this date, making it a complete document of the performance [1].",
